# Cursor Rules for Meeting Copilot Architectural Refactor

## Dependency Rules
- core: only imports core/types; NO React or DOM.
- infrastructure: imports core, lib, common.
- services: imports core + infrastructure/ipc. STRICTLY NO React or ReactDOM imports. Each service folder has a public index.ts.
- hooks/components/features: import services, core, lib, components/ui, infrastructure/ipc.
- components/ui & lib: only import lib.
- features: must NOT import internal files of another feature (features/<other>/*), only through public index.ts.
- IPC: All window.api calls MUST go through typed ports in @/infrastructure/ipc. Direct window.api calls are prohibited.

## Size Limits
- Container component: <= 600 lines
- Custom hook: <= 300 lines and <= ~8 useState
- Sub-component: <= 400 lines
- Service file: <= ~500 lines

## Implementation Rules
- Never use state+ref mirrors (const r = useRef(val); r.current = val; in render). Use useLatest(val).
- Timers must go through shared hooks (useTimeout, useInterval).
- Pure logic (debounce, dedupe, queues, loops, state machines) written in pure TS controllers; hooks only wire.
- Invariants: ZERO UI/UX changes, ZERO string literal changes, ZERO runtime dependencies added, ZERO IPC contract modifications.

